    "canonical": "Terminate TCP and SSL at a Layer 7 reverse-proxy/edge front end close to the user (forwarding to backends over long-lived, pre-warmed encrypted connections) to minimize HTTPS handshake round trips and to mitigate low-level attacks a packet-level balancer cannot."
